Find an hour and do it
for an hour every day

00:22:47.969 --> 00:22:49.349
to get to the answer.

00:22:49.349 --> 00:22:51.655
And then also understand that
the first 10 times you do it,

00:22:51.655 --> 00:22:53.139
it might not be right.

00:22:53.139 --> 00:22:54.141
Because it's like,

00:22:54.141 --> 00:22:55.744
you know I always talk about the ROI.

00:22:55.744 --> 00:22:57.904
People are like, "what's
the ROI of influencers or VR

00:22:57.904 --> 00:23:01.537
the ROI of those 10 hours
reaching out to influencers?".

00:23:01.537 --> 00:23:05.770
The ROI of a basketball is
very different to people.

00:23:05.770 --> 00:23:07.043
To me it's nothing,

00:23:07.043 --> 00:23:09.242
to LeBron James, it's a billion dollars.

00:23:09.242 --> 00:23:12.036
So all this stuff works.

00:23:12.036 --> 00:23:14.221
It's "are you good at it?",

00:23:14.221 --> 00:23:16.033
is a whole 'nother question.

00:23:16.033 --> 00:23:18.878
So it's not just the ROI of trying it

00:23:18.878 --> 00:23:20.662
then you got to get good at it.

00:23:20.662 --> 00:23:22.159
Nothing you're good at right now,

00:23:22.159 --> 00:23:25.332
you were so great out the
first time you tried it.

00:23:25.332 --> 00:23:27.529
So, of course, man.

00:23:27.529 --> 00:23:29.301
Like everything that's happening,

00:23:29.301 --> 00:23:31.727
you need to figure out how
it works for your business,

00:23:31.727 --> 00:23:33.809
B to B, B to C, personal brand.

00:23:33.809 --> 00:23:35.065
The question is,

00:23:35.065 --> 00:23:38.318
what are you doing with
your time, you know?

00:23:38.318 --> 00:23:40.800
And so that's why I get mad at people

00:23:40.800 --> 00:23:42.554
who wanna be an entrepreneur

00:23:42.554 --> 00:23:45.998
and watch four hours of
Netflix a weekend or,

00:23:45.998 --> 00:23:47.101
and by the way,

00:23:47.101 --> 00:23:48.090
people need escapism,

00:23:48.090 --> 00:23:48.965
you need to check out,

00:23:48.965 --> 00:23:49.830
you need to rest,

00:23:49.830 --> 00:23:51.287
you have to be in a mental place.

00:23:51.287 --> 00:23:53.605
But the scrutiny that we
have to put on our time

00:23:53.605 --> 00:23:55.795
as young entrepreneurs, you know,

00:23:55.795 --> 00:23:58.075
it's just time or money.

00:23:58.075 --> 00:23:59.739
Talent is the variable that sits in here,

00:23:59.739 --> 00:24:02.244
but the assets that you're sitting with

00:24:02.244 --> 00:24:04.070
in the beginning are time

00:24:04.070 --> 00:24:06.540
and then you amass money and
then you can use the money

00:24:06.540 --> 00:24:09.198
to save time and you're
just going back and forth.

00:24:09.198 --> 00:24:11.546
And everybody wants these big dreams

00:24:11.546 --> 00:24:14.043
and they're not willing to
work at the level they need to

00:24:14.043 --> 00:24:16.178
and that's the advantage they have.

00:24:16.178 --> 00:24:18.261
So, fuck yes, you should.

00:24:19.164 --> 00:24:20.037
- I just want to wrap it up

00:24:20.037 --> 00:24:21.197
and that's the biggest inspiration

00:24:21.197 --> 00:24:23.655
I got from you since 2014.

00:24:23.655 --> 00:24:26.555
Just to cut off the crap
and just fucking work.

00:24:26.555 --> 00:24:27.516
So thank you so much.

00:24:27.516 --> 00:24:29.435
- You're welcome and I
just wanna say one thing.

00:24:29.435 --> 00:24:31.063
If that's your ambition,

00:24:31.063 --> 00:24:33.166
you can work 10 hours a week.

00:24:33.166 --> 00:24:35.584
If you're happy, I'm happy.

00:24:35.584 --> 00:24:37.477
But don't go running around saying

00:24:37.477 --> 00:24:40.068
you're gonna build a 17
million dollar business

00:24:40.068 --> 00:24:43.427
and think you're gonna do
that on 25 hours a week.

00:24:43.427 --> 00:24:45.601
That person doesn't exist.

00:24:45.601 --> 00:24:47.560
Anybody you know who's
built something meaningful,

00:24:47.560 --> 00:24:49.311
has worked for it.

00:24:49.311 --> 00:24:51.339
I know people have inherited money,

00:24:51.339 --> 00:24:53.103
but they're not the one that built it.

00:24:53.103 --> 00:24:55.076
Anybody you know that built something,

00:24:55.076 --> 00:24:56.372
put in the work.

00:24:56.372 --> 00:24:57.205
There's just no shortcut.

00:24:57.205 --> 00:24:58.587
It's like working out.

00:24:58.587 --> 00:25:01.232
You can't think about pushups.

00:25:01.232 --> 00:25:04.280
(light laughter)

00:25:04.280 --> 00:25:05.157
Good.

00:25:05.157 --> 00:25:06.129
(applause)

00:25:06.129 --> 00:25:07.129
- Thank you.

00:25:13.299 --> 00:25:15.851
- [Host] And before we
take the next question,

00:25:15.851 --> 00:25:19.042
you can begin to wonder if
you want to ask Gary something

00:25:19.042 --> 00:25:22.792
because we got a few
more questions prepared.

00:25:24.083 --> 00:25:26.819
But then it's up to you, the audience.

00:25:26.819 --> 00:25:27.652
- Awesome.

00:25:27.652 --> 00:25:29.434
- [Host] So, yeah?

00:25:29.434 --> 00:25:31.932
In a while we'll set you free.

00:25:31.932 --> 00:25:32.765
Jonas.

00:25:33.673 --> 00:25:34.506
- Yeah I'm here.

00:25:34.506 --> 00:25:35.506
- Over here?

00:25:36.656 --> 00:25:38.309
- How are you Jonas?

00:25:38.309 --> 00:25:40.347
- Oh shit, I can't believe
I'm talking to you, man.

00:25:40.347 --> 00:25:41.180
(laughs)

00:25:41.180 --> 00:25:42.261
(audience laughs)

00:25:42.261 --> 00:25:43.094
- Don't worry brother,

00:25:43.094 --> 00:25:44.099
it's gonna be okay.

00:25:44.099 --> 00:25:46.349
(applause)

00:25:48.949 --> 00:25:50.105
- All right, so my question is

00:25:50.105 --> 00:25:53.620
in the very, very early
stage of the startup,

00:25:53.620 --> 00:25:54.453
my first startup,

00:25:54.453 --> 00:25:55.397
- Yep.

00:25:55.397 --> 00:25:57.328
- And on the very, very slight budget.

00:25:57.328 --> 00:25:58.161
- Yep.

00:25:58.161 --> 00:25:59.931
- The first thing to focus on,

00:25:59.931 --> 00:26:03.588
the most important thing and how to.

00:26:03.588 --> 00:26:05.223
- (sighs) There's so much brother, so --

00:26:05.223 --> 00:26:06.276
- I'm so overwhelming,

00:26:06.276 --> 00:26:07.166
that's why I'm asking you.

00:26:07.166 --> 00:26:09.488
- Of course, I mean I think a lot

00:26:09.488 --> 00:26:10.353
of what I just talked about is true.

00:26:10.353 --> 00:26:14.832
The biggest advantage you
have right now is your time.

00:26:14.832 --> 00:26:16.551
It's your number one asset.

00:26:16.551 --> 00:26:17.546
You're young,

00:26:17.546 --> 00:26:18.747
you should have plenty of energy,

00:26:18.747 --> 00:26:19.580
you're hungry,

00:26:19.580 --> 00:26:20.988
you're ambitious, great.

00:26:20.988 --> 00:26:23.362
You need to work every
goddamn minute you can.

00:26:23.362 --> 00:26:25.713
It's the single biggest thing you've got.

00:26:25.713 --> 00:26:26.546
The other thing is

00:26:26.546 --> 00:26:28.708
you need to figure out how
to get leverage, right?

00:26:28.708 --> 00:26:31.501
So, you need to figure
out what does that mean?

00:26:31.501 --> 00:26:33.501
So, what's the business?

00:26:34.384 --> 00:26:37.745
- Right now it's a
website selling posters.

00:26:37.745 --> 00:26:38.740
- It's a what, brother?

00:26:38.740 --> 00:26:40.871
- A web shop selling posters.

00:26:40.871 --> 00:26:42.475
- A web shop selling posters?

00:26:42.475 --> 00:26:43.624
- Yeah, yeah.

00:26:43.624 --> 00:26:44.687
- So, you're a web shop,

00:26:44.687 --> 00:26:47.149
when you say posters,

00:26:47.149 --> 00:26:48.457
you, physical?

00:26:48.457 --> 00:26:49.290
- Yeah.

00:26:49.290 --> 00:26:51.898
- Okay, so you're trying
to sell them to people?

00:26:51.898 --> 00:26:53.210
- Yeah.

00:26:53.210 --> 00:26:57.269
- And how much does it
cost you to make them?

00:26:57.269 --> 00:26:59.367
- 10 bucks, right now.

00:26:59.367 --> 00:27:02.481
It's in very small pieces again, package.

00:27:02.481 --> 00:27:05.652
- So, one thing that I'm a
huge fan of in the beginning

00:27:05.652 --> 00:27:07.878
is doing a lot of work for free.

00:27:07.878 --> 00:27:09.999
And people get very mad
at me for this advice.

00:27:09.999 --> 00:27:11.375
I don't know why.

00:27:11.375 --> 00:27:13.345
'Cause they debate me in theory

00:27:13.345 --> 00:27:16.042
instead of actually
ever living a business.

00:27:16.042 --> 00:27:17.749
You know, one of the things

00:27:17.749 --> 00:27:19.323
that you're looking for is awareness.

00:27:19.323 --> 00:27:21.766
You need to let people know you exist.

00:27:21.766 --> 00:27:23.285
One of the great ways to do that

00:27:23.285 --> 00:27:26.651
is to do free work for
people that have awareness.

00:27:26.651 --> 00:27:27.989
You're giving them work,

00:27:27.989 --> 00:27:29.880
they're giving you awareness.

00:27:29.880 --> 00:27:31.955
So I would have a hardcore
strategy in the market

00:27:31.955 --> 00:27:33.574
that you're trying to fulfill,

00:27:33.574 --> 00:27:35.792
to do free work and reach
out to the companies

00:27:35.792 --> 00:27:37.016
or individuals and say,

00:27:37.016 --> 00:27:40.392
I wanna do this for you for
free because I like your work.

00:27:40.392 --> 00:27:42.025
This is the kind of work we do,

00:27:42.025 --> 00:27:42.969
would you like it?

00:27:42.969 --> 00:27:44.119
And by the way,

00:27:44.119 --> 00:27:47.546
I have a thousand people
a day offer me "free"

00:27:47.546 --> 00:27:48.841
and I don't take them up on it

00:27:48.841 --> 00:27:51.662
because the value exchange
of the time is not worth it.

00:27:51.662 --> 00:27:53.366
So just 'cause you even offer it for free

00:27:53.366 --> 00:27:54.714
doesn't mean they'll take you up on it.

00:27:54.714 --> 00:27:56.368
But the number one thing I would do first,

00:27:56.368 --> 00:27:57.201
if I was your partner,

00:27:57.201 --> 00:27:58.034
I was like,

00:27:58.034 --> 00:27:59.196
cool, let's get side jobs,

00:27:59.196 --> 00:28:00.383
let's sell shit.

00:28:00.383 --> 00:28:02.474
Let's do something else to amass dollars,

00:28:02.474 --> 00:28:03.595
let's borrow money,

00:28:03.595 --> 00:28:04.428
let's rent money,

00:28:04.428 --> 00:28:06.401
let's raise capital or
let's take our money

00:28:06.401 --> 00:28:08.159
that we have together
to do as much free work

00:28:08.159 --> 00:28:09.801
for the biggest celebrity,

00:28:09.801 --> 00:28:10.750
the biggest athlete,

00:28:10.750 --> 00:28:12.345
the biggest business, the coolest thing,

00:28:12.345 --> 00:28:16.862
the coolest festival,
the coolest brand, free,

00:28:16.862 --> 00:28:20.034
as long as we're getting
awareness out of it,

00:28:20.034 --> 00:28:23.356
to build our brand to
then create deal flow.

00:28:23.356 --> 00:28:24.785
- All right, do you
think that's possible to

00:28:24.785 --> 00:28:27.095
with a very tight budget.

00:28:27.095 --> 00:28:29.661
So, you're meaning that I
have to work free for them

00:28:29.661 --> 00:28:31.823
or then I have to provide
some of my products

00:28:31.823 --> 00:28:32.656
for them, for free?

00:28:32.656 --> 00:28:33.489
- Both.

00:28:33.489 --> 00:28:34.322
- Both?

00:28:34.322 --> 00:28:35.155
- Free and free.

00:28:35.155 --> 00:28:35.988
- Yeah.

00:28:35.988 --> 00:28:38.443
- Which could mean that you
may have to get a side job

00:28:38.443 --> 00:28:40.940
at night or borrow money

00:28:40.940 --> 00:28:44.300
or have a separate business all together,

00:28:44.300 --> 00:28:48.609
but, or do services for
other people at low costs.

00:28:48.609 --> 00:28:51.934
Like, what I get surprised
that people don't understand,

00:28:51.934 --> 00:28:54.977
is what are the alternatives?

00:28:54.977 --> 00:28:57.219
Like, why are you asking me this question?

00:28:57.219 --> 00:28:59.497
You're asking 'cause you don't
have the answer right now,

00:28:59.497 --> 00:29:01.079
because there's not that many alternatives

00:29:01.079 --> 00:29:02.319
when you don't have a lot of money

00:29:02.319 --> 00:29:05.293
and nobody knows what
the fuck your product is.

00:29:05.293 --> 00:29:06.411
(snickers)

00:29:06.411 --> 00:29:07.244
- Yeah, exactly.

00:29:07.244 --> 00:29:11.133
- Right, so, entrepreneurship is super fun

00:29:11.133 --> 00:29:12.483
and cool on Instagram,

00:29:12.483 --> 00:29:14.837
but in real life, it sucks shit.

00:29:14.837 --> 00:29:15.830
(laughter)

00:29:15.830 --> 00:29:19.691
So, you know, doing shit
for free is not fun.

00:29:19.691 --> 00:29:20.524
Go ahead.

00:29:20.524 --> 00:29:22.446
- I'm just saying that I have
a part-time job right now.

00:29:22.446 --> 00:29:23.279
- That's good.

00:29:23.279 --> 00:29:26.618
- Yeah, and I'm working
on this after hours and --

00:29:26.618 --> 00:29:28.077
- Great, so you know the money --

00:29:28.077 --> 00:29:30.562
- You just want me to use all the money

00:29:30.562 --> 00:29:31.438
for the business, right?

00:29:31.438 --> 00:29:34.083
- Yes, so don't buy another thing.

00:29:34.083 --> 00:29:36.583
No more nice jacket.

00:29:36.583 --> 00:29:37.607
- That's from my mom, so.

00:29:37.607 --> 00:29:38.440
- Respect.

00:29:38.440 --> 00:29:40.404
(laughter)

00:29:40.404 --> 00:29:41.237
(applause)

00:29:41.237 --> 00:29:42.709
That's good. That's good.

00:29:42.709 --> 00:29:46.709
Yeah, I think a small
company that makes posters

00:29:47.574 --> 00:29:49.519
number one arbitrage,

00:29:49.519 --> 00:29:51.589
is to make posters for free

00:29:51.589 --> 00:29:53.521
for things that will give them awareness.

00:29:53.521 --> 00:29:54.510
When people are like,

00:29:54.510 --> 00:29:55.343
"who made that poster?",

00:29:55.343 --> 00:29:56.281
if your brand's there,

00:29:56.281 --> 00:29:57.114
things of that nature,

00:29:57.114 --> 00:30:00.330
that is your number one move
you can do when you're tiny.

00:30:00.330 --> 00:30:02.315
And so you just need to
be able to afford that,

00:30:02.315 --> 00:30:06.635
including selling the nice
jacket that your mom gave you.

00:30:06.635 --> 00:30:09.968
(laughter and applause)

00:30:13.857 --> 00:30:14.690
- Thank you man.

00:30:14.690 --> 00:30:16.811
- You're welcome.

00:30:16.811 --> 00:30:19.384
- [Host] Okay, Miguel, where are you?

00:30:19.384 --> 00:30:20.217
- But you know what?

00:30:20.217 --> 00:30:21.958
Real quick because it's a funny moment,

00:30:21.958 --> 00:30:23.603
it's just very true.

00:30:23.603 --> 00:30:27.900
Like, there's a reason
immigrants over-index in success.

00:30:27.900 --> 00:30:30.001
That's the kind of shit they do.

00:30:30.001 --> 00:30:31.314
They don't buy anything.

00:30:31.314 --> 00:30:35.133
They live in a place that has
a shitty house for seven years

00:30:35.133 --> 00:30:36.033
and save every dollar

00:30:36.033 --> 00:30:38.627
even though they could've
moved out two years earlier

00:30:38.627 --> 00:30:39.778
or four years earlier.

00:30:39.778 --> 00:30:42.556
Non-entrepreneurs, as soon
as they get a little money,

00:30:42.556 --> 00:30:43.664
buy dumb shit,

00:30:43.664 --> 00:30:47.226
instead of putting it
back into their business.

00:30:47.226 --> 00:30:49.281
And so like, it seems like a funny joke,

00:30:49.281 --> 00:30:51.549
but like, when you have no options,

00:30:51.549 --> 00:30:53.464
you have no options.

00:30:53.464 --> 00:30:55.522
Like it's not miraculously gonna happen

00:30:55.522 --> 00:30:59.461
and everybody got tricked because
of venture capital funding

00:30:59.461 --> 00:31:01.015
and everybody thinks they're
gonna writer a business plan

00:31:01.015 --> 00:31:04.287
on paper and go out and
find some miraculous VC

00:31:04.287 --> 00:31:05.596
and then they complain,

00:31:05.596 --> 00:31:08.606
well in Denmark and Norway
they don't have good VCs,

00:31:08.606 --> 00:31:09.671
but Silicon Valley,

00:31:09.671 --> 00:31:12.357
Silicon Valley's a fuckin' bitch too.

00:31:12.357 --> 00:31:13.332
They'll take the meeting,

00:31:13.332 --> 00:31:15.517
but not gonna give you money either.

00:31:15.517 --> 00:31:18.498
And so, we need to be
smart and more practical.

00:31:18.498 --> 00:31:19.915
That's real life.

00:31:22.336 --> 00:31:23.319
- [Host] Thank you.

00:31:23.319 --> 00:31:24.839
- You're welcome.

00:31:24.839 --> 00:31:27.089
(applause)

00:31:29.323 --> 00:31:31.043
- [Host] Okay, Miguel where are you?

00:31:31.043 --> 00:31:32.807
Down here, can we get a mic now?

00:31:32.807 --> 00:31:33.683
- Smack in the middle.

00:31:33.683 --> 00:31:34.641
- [Host] Yeah.

00:31:34.641 --> 00:31:35.883
- Hey Miguel.

00:31:35.883 --> 00:31:36.716
- Oh my god.

00:31:36.716 --> 00:31:39.109
Gary V. is in the house and
I'm about to ask a question.

00:31:39.109 --> 00:31:39.942
- Yes you are.

00:31:39.942 --> 00:31:41.466
- Okay, hi Gary, is it possible --

00:31:41.466 --> 00:31:42.299
- How are you?

00:31:42.299 --> 00:31:43.904
- Very good.

00:31:43.904 --> 00:31:46.303
If you're about to open a
trampoline park in Copenhagen

00:31:46.303 --> 00:31:47.346
in around four month,

00:31:47.346 --> 00:31:48.895
how would you approach the marketing

00:31:48.895 --> 00:31:51.310
until the opening and after?

00:31:51.310 --> 00:31:53.539
- Okay, let's start with the four months.

00:31:53.539 --> 00:31:56.400
Is that an arbitrary thing
or is that a 100% locked in?

00:31:56.400 --> 00:31:58.265
Like, why four months?

00:31:58.265 --> 00:31:59.813
- Had a meeting with the owner, the boss,

00:31:59.813 --> 00:32:02.152
yesterday and he wants me to run it,

00:32:02.152 --> 00:32:04.851
but he want to do the
marketing and I ask him,

00:32:04.851 --> 00:32:06.252
what would you do?

00:32:06.252 --> 00:32:09.344
Facebook ads and Google ads and that's it.

00:32:09.344 --> 00:32:10.423
- That's what you asked him?

00:32:10.423 --> 00:32:12.459
- Yes, he would do the marketing

00:32:12.459 --> 00:32:15.740
with Facebook ads and Google ads.

00:32:15.740 --> 00:32:16.674
- And that's what he wants to do?

00:32:16.674 --> 00:32:17.603
- That's it.

00:32:17.603 --> 00:32:18.436
- Okay.

00:32:18.436 --> 00:32:19.839
- And what would you do?

00:32:19.839 --> 00:32:21.923
- I'm very high on that.

00:32:21.923 --> 00:32:24.531
You know, I kind of did a
little bit of homework on

00:32:24.531 --> 00:32:26.255
like the attention arbitrage in Copenhagen

00:32:26.255 --> 00:32:27.091
before I got here.

00:32:27.091 --> 00:32:28.429
I think that's cool.

00:32:28.429 --> 00:32:31.330
I would just add influencer
marketing on top of that.

00:32:31.330 --> 00:32:33.303
I think there's a lot
of Instagram, Snapchat,

00:32:33.303 --> 00:32:35.154
Facebook personalities that could bring

00:32:35.154 --> 00:32:39.024
disproportionate attention
to this and are under-priced.

00:32:39.024 --> 00:32:41.723
It's incredible to me that
there's a lot of individuals

00:32:41.723 --> 00:32:45.397
in the Copenhagen metro area and suburbs

00:32:45.397 --> 00:32:48.064
that you could invite for free,

00:32:48.064 --> 00:32:50.607
